%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% Scenario: capture nests. A form's procedure fills with a pattern: the
% pattern resource belongs to the page, its matrix maps pattern space
% to the form's space, and the fill inside the form resource names it.
% The same instance then fills on the page itself, which is a second
% pattern resource over the same cell with the page's matrix.
/P << /PatternType 1 /PaintType 1 /TilingType 1 /BBox [0 0 10 10]
  /XStep 10 /YStep 10 /PaintProc { pop 0 0 5 5 rectfill } >>
  matrix makepattern def
/F << /FormType 1 /BBox [0 0 100 100] /Matrix [1 0 0 1 50 50]
  /PaintProc { pop P setpattern 0 0 100 100 rectfill } >> def
F execform
P setpattern
300 300 100 100 rectfill
showpage
